# Auth tokens for the Sandcastle loop — copy to .sandcastle/.env.secrets and fill in.
#
#   cp .sandcastle/.env.secrets.example .sandcastle/.env.secrets
#
# ⚠ Auth tokens live HERE, in .env.secrets — NEVER in .env.
# Sandcastle's resolveEnv merges ALL of .env into every sandbox, and a sandbox env
# can only add keys, never remove them. Two tokens in .env would both leak into
# every sandbox → claude-code sends the wrong token to the wrong base URL → 401.
# .env.secrets is gitignored and read only by main.ts, which bakes one token per
# sandbox based on the active profile.
#
# Only the tokens the ACTIVE PROFILE's providers need are required. The defaults
# (config.ts) are the Split profile: zai (GLM/z.ai) implementer/planner + anthropic
# (Opus) reviewer, so both tokens below are needed. An Opus-only profile
# (SANDCASTLE_PROFILE=opus) needs only the Anthropic one. main.ts validates the
# required tokens at startup, not at the first sandbox.

# Provider "zai" — GLM via z.ai (Anthropic-compatible endpoint).
# Used by the planner + implementer in the Split profile.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Provider "anthropic" — Anthropic direct (api.anthropic.com).
# Used by the reviewer in the Split profile, and by every role in the Opus profile.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
